  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A simple pendulum of length $L$ swings in a vertical plane. The tension of the string when it makes an angle $\\theta$ with the vertical and the bob of mass $m$ moves with a speed $v$ is $\\mathrm{fg}$ is the gravitational acceleration)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DJBVY",
      "text": "$m v^{2} / L$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5x5Qb",
      "text": "$m g \\cos \\theta+m v^{2} / L$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aPaGl",
      "text": "$m g \\cos \\theta-m v^{2} / L$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4lxHS",
      "text": "$m g \\cos \\theta$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The situation is given below\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2015_phy_a5.png\">\r\n\r\nFor motion along a vertical circular track, the required centripetal force is along the radius and towards the centre of the circle is given by $T-m g \\cos \\theta=\\frac{m v^{2}}{L}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad T=\\frac{m v^{2}}{L}+m g \\cos \\theta$",
    "image": null
